# No em dashes

Do not use the em dash character (U+2014) anywhere in this repo: PHP, Vue, TypeScript, comments, UI copy, docs, tests, or commit messages this agent writes.

Do not use an en dash (U+2013) as a stand-in for that same "fancy dash" in prose or UI strings.

Use a comma, a period, a colon, or ASCII hyphen-minus `-` instead.

```text
BAD:  Save the record — then reload.
BAD:  Save the record – then reload.
GOOD: Save the record, then reload.
GOOD: Save the record. Then reload.
GOOD: Prefix: value
GOOD: 2024-08-15
```

Hyphen-minus in identifiers, flags, URLs, and ISO dates is required (`view-any`, `--help`, `en-GB`).
